# Harness

A single-binary Windows CLI tool written in Go that attaches to an **existing Gemini web conversation** (including chats started with your custom Gems), uploads images from `.data-harness-gemini-in/`, sends prompts serially one-by-one, and saves each response to `.data-harness-gemini-out/<tag>.md`.

## Prerequisites

1. **Go 1.23+** installed on your machine (`go version`).
2. **Google Chrome** installed on your Windows machine.
3. An **existing Gemini chat URL** (e.g., `https://gemini.google.com/app/1234567890abcdef`).

## Folder Setup

Ensure your `harness/` directory looks like this before running:

```text
harness/
├── go.mod
├── main.go
├── README.md
└── .data-harness-gemini-in/
    ├── human-prompts.json
    ├── image1.png
    ├── image2.jpg
    └── image3.png